text.section:
Upon application of, or in a proceeding commenced by, a person specified in subsection B, the circuit court in the county or city in which the principal office of the corporation is located, or, if none in the Commonwealth, in the county or city in which its registered office is located may determine:

The result or validity of the election, appointment, removal, or resignation of a director or officer of the corporation;


The right of an individual to hold the office of director or officer of the corporation;


The result or validity of any vote by the shareholders of the corporation;


The right of a director to membership on a committee of the board of directors; and


The right of a person to nominate, or an individual to be nominated as, a candidate for election or appointment as a director of the corporation, and any right under a bylaw adopted pursuant to subsection C of § 13.1-624 or any comparable right under any provision of the articles of incorporation, a contract, or applicable law.

Any application or proceeding pursuant to subsection A may be filed or commenced by any of the following persons:

The corporation;


A record shareholder, beneficial shareholder or unrestricted voting trust beneficial owner of the corporation;


A director of the corporation, an individual claiming the office of director, or a director whose membership on a committee of the board of directors is contested, who, in each case, is seeking a determination of the individual's right to such office or membership;


An officer of the corporation or an individual claiming to be an officer of the corporation, in each case who is seeking a determination of the individual's right to such office; or


A person claiming a right covered by subdivision A 5 and who is seeking a determination of such right.

In connection with any application or proceeding under subsection A, the following shall be named as defendants, unless such person made the application or commenced the proceeding:

The corporation;


An individual whose right to office or membership on a committee of the board of directors is contested;


Any individual claiming the office or membership at issue; and


Any person claiming a right covered by subdivision A 5 that is at issue.

In connection with any application or proceeding under subsection A, the court shall dispose of the application or proceeding on an expedited basis and also may:

Order such additional or further notice as the court deems proper under the circumstances;


Order that additional persons be joined as parties to the proceeding if the court determines that such joinder is necessary for a just adjudication of matters before the court;


Order an election or meeting be held in accordance with the provisions of § 13.1-656 or otherwise;


Appoint a master to conduct an election or meeting;


Enter temporary, preliminary, or permanent injunctive relief;


Resolve solely for the purpose of the proceeding any legal or factual issues necessary for the resolution of any of the matters specified in subsection A, including the right and power of persons claiming to own shares to vote at any meeting of the shareholders; and


Order such relief as the court determines is equitable, just, and proper.
